{"abstract":"This paper explores how participatory design methods can engage future farmers in imagining sustainable agricultural futures in Denmark. Denmark's agricultural sector faces a \"crisis of imagination\" where dominant paradigms in farming are hard to challenge. Building on Ingold's notion of the landscape as a relational, temporal space for dwelling, we propose a conceptualization of the landscape game that enables farming students to articulate their visions of future farming. The design game creates opportunities for participants to situate their imagined farms within broader social, environmental, and technical contexts while exploring how these might evolve over time. This approach aims to generate new agricultural imaginaries that move beyond current techno-solutionist or radical transformation narratives, while supporting an underrepresented political public in developing their own perspective on contested agricultural futures that are both speculative and grounded in lived experience.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828153"],"event":{"acronym":"Nordes","title":"Nordic Design Research Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agriculture","Design Games","Farming","Futuring","Landscape"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"re imagining the landscape of future farming","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2025.26","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828153","ids":["itu-5905bdb8-26cc-4b0e-a5f8-d436c0243fb9"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Design games","Farming","Futuring","Landscape"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-47CDD481D8D9CB08F892C1277BB571EC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/nordes.2025.26","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/112678574/Re-Imagining_the_Landscape_of_Future_Farming.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/nordes.2025.26","publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","title":"Nordic Design Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5905bdb8-26cc-4b0e-a5f8-d436c0243fb9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Re-Imagining the Landscape of Future Farming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828153","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Prototyping is a complex process of navigating a chaotic design space. Especially when there are few criteria for success, it is often difficult for a designer to know what direction to follow. We argue that prototyping can be considered as a process of sensemaking driven by finding the right expression of a design goal. To illustrate this, we present the case study of the aural-visualiser 1000, a functional refined prototype that resulted from an open-ended design project. Using its process as an example, we abstract important expressions that informed the design and prototyping of the aural-visualiser 1000, pointing to when the conception of the project changed and how that affected our making sense of the design space. We reflect on this design process to articulate productive pivots and tensions that led to the finished artefact.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718851"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Expression","Listening","Presence","Prototyping","Sensemaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prototyping as making sense of expressions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700224/2023_Padalak_Jenkins_Prototyping_as_making_sene_of_expressions.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718851","ids":["itu-4907f5e7-06f2-406b-aabe-1b780a6167b3"],"keyword":["Prototyping","expression","listening","presence","sensemaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2928EE14D3F97251F56E9734F9454B39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/100700224/2023_Padalak_Jenkins_Prototyping_as_making_sene_of_expressions.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Design Research Society","status":"p","subtitle":"From Abstractness to Concreteness","title":"EKSIG 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4907f5e7-06f2-406b-aabe-1b780a6167b3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prototyping as making sense of expressions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718851","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The aural-visualiser 1000 is a prototype that reorients a user towards understanding the world from an auditory perspective instead of a primarily visual one. By attending to everyday audio instead of vision, the device asks the user to pay attention to the world in a more embodied way. Developed as a means of experimenting with the capacity of physical interaction design to support being present in the world differently, it records audio from everyday life and creates mementos for later reflection and interpretation. The mementos, paper receipts with abstract sound visualizations on them, offer a means of remembering experiences as they were to be there, instead of as they were recorded through image or video.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Gehrchen, Thea Emilie","Hansen, Søren Smedegaard","Pedersen, Peter Langgard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382659"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["RtD attention presence senses images interaction design aes thetics expressions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aural visualiser 000000001000 physical interaction design for materializing moments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114792/nordichiadjunct22_48.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382659","identifier":[{"id":"85139872027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5ccd4eb5-1d7b-4986-bf6c-5e24ab5694d8"],"keyword":["RtD, attention, presence, senses, images, interaction design, aes- thetics, expressions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4DFB09B2AD7E24FB98DB9900AEF51C00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114792/nordichiadjunct22_48.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea Emilie","key":"gehrchenpau","last":"Gehrchen","name":"Gehrchen, Thea Emilie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Smedegaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Søren Smedegaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Langgard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Peter Langgard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3547522.3547722","isbn":["9781450394482"],"pages":"1-3","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Adjunct Proceedings of the 2022 Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139872027"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5ccd4eb5-1d7b-4986-bf6c-5e24ab5694d8"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"aural-visualiser 1000: physical interaction design for materializing moments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382659","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aural-visualiser 1000 is an interactive system for recording the world around you. Like a camera that captures sounds instead of images, it is meant to develop memories that are focused on what it was like to be in a moment. Aural-visualiser 1000 critiques an image-centered society, particularly how the image has become the dominant form of representing human experience. Collections of photos have become a replacement memory that end up never being looked at. Often, taking a photograph or finding the right angle for a video replaces being present in the world. Focusing on audio requires a user to relate to their world and engage actively in finding things worth noticing. In creating a memento from the sound, av1000 records a memory that can be reviewed later. This requires active participation to reconstruct a meaningful experience. The system argues for interaction design that goes beyond tapping fingers on glass towards exploring the surrounding world intentionally.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384268"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Attention presence senses images interaction design RtD"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"being in the world with the aural visualiser 000000001000","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140883379","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384268","identifier":[{"id":"85140883379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cd1a7a2f-8626-45e4-93a6-80bc3ead406b"],"keyword":["Attention, presence, senses, images, interaction design, RtD"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-59546C5A1C36C3811822D4E40C3674AD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Abildgaard","key":"padalakpau","last":"Padalak","locid":"17ebd58d-ffad-4a6f-923d-a0118d0056b0","name":"Padalak, Martin Abildgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3547281","isbn":["9781450396998"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140883379"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd1a7a2f-8626-45e4-93a6-80bc3ead406b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Being in the world with the aural-visualiser 1000","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384268","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
